# Build artifacts.
#
# The bulk of build/ is object files + CMake state (~900 MB) and is regenerated, so it stays
# ignored. build/bin is the exception and MUST stay tracked:
#   * scripts/check_build_tracked.sh (installed as .git/hooks/pre-commit) FAILS a commit when
#     any build/bin dylib / symlink target is not tracked -- the project once lost a 29.85 t/s
#     build because a rebuild silently overwrote an untracked dylib, and a checkout is supposed
#     to be runnable/verifiable without rebuilding.
#   * a bare `build/` rule swallows build/bin too, which silently defeats that gate (it reports
#     every dylib as untracked). Do NOT put `build/` back here; use the `build/*` + negation
#     pair below, which ignores the directory contents one level down while re-including bin/.
# Negation cannot resurrect a path whose parent directory is excluded, which is why the parent
# is matched with `build/*` (children only) instead of the whole `build/` tree.
build/*
!build/bin/
